## Scientific And Domain Assessments

### cerium(III) nitrate hexahydrate — complete source candidate transition

identity: supported. Targets: ORIGINAL-w02::c-proposal-cerium-nitrate-hexahydrate.

MediaDive 1587 supplies the parenthesized Ce(NO3)3 x 6 H2O formula and CAS10294-41-4; PubChem CID16211466 independently corroborates cerium(III) nitrate hexahydrate, CeH12N3O15, mass434.22 and the exact supplied InChI. The exact-form CAS identity, six waters and Ce(III) oxidation state are supported. The MeSH Concept M0319657 is the broader Ce(III) nitrate target; NARROW_MATCH must retain skos:broadMatch, not exactMatch or subclass_of. Changing the malformed flattened token to REJECTED_LABEL preserves its source evidence while preventing it from resolving as an approved chemical synonym. The corrected provider token is retained as RAW_TEXT; prior history and occurrence statistics are preserved. The payload corrects the earlier unresolved formula/CAS gap with inspected evidence and explicitly withdraws inherited publication support; its proposed MAPPED status is not itself native review approval.

Retained limits: No exact ChEBI claim or assertion that no exact ontology term exists globally. Captured searches have bounded coverage; the unsupported CAS web response is not CAS-authority corroboration. Sigma product comparison is evidence of material identity only, not procurement of the original recipe. No supplier, catalogue, lot, purity or role is assigned to the source. MediaDive's nominal0.06g/L belongs to a stock solution; DSMZ specifies per litre water, not a measured final stock volume. No final-medium dose, or approval of flattened medium occurrences, follows. Do not promote all PubChem synonym strings: the captured list also contains solution/grade wording beyond this exact hydrate. No Cerium export-source binding is introduced in the four-source/five-occurrence export canary. Future stable adoption must preserve assigned MIM:0002742 and typed legacy record aliases; the rejected bare label must stay non-resolving. This preparation does not execute that continuity proof.

