### Arabinan from Sugar Beet — complete source candidate transition

identity: supported. Targets: ORIGINAL-w03::m-arabinan_source_alias.

The added raw label preserves the same sugar-beet botanical qualifier and arabinan material head noun as the complete owner. Captured manufacturer text names sugar-beet arabinan; captured ChEBI22590 denotes the broader arabinan polysaccharide class. Existing cas:11078-27-6 identifier, NARROW_MATCH grade and asymmetric CHEBI22590 mapping are unchanged; no exact generic-parent or subclass relation is added.

Retained limits: The archived manufacturer artifact is a webtool response with extracted primary page/data-sheet content, not raw PDF bytes or a newly retrieved primary document. P-ARAB and linear/debranched P-LARB share CAS11078-27-6 in the capture; this is not unique grade identity. No supplier procurement, branching, lot, purity, structure or generic-arabinan exactness is newly approved. Historical record statements about absence of an exact ChEBI term and CultureBotHT CAS provenance are retained, not independently re-established by this alias-only transition preparation. Keep the full frozen 0.2%w/v alternative-use context; adding the alias grants no role, recipe, source-identity or export approval. Future current native external review must retain actual broadMatch semantics, separate from any MIM identity; no subclass edge follows.

