### Barley grains — complete source candidate transition

identity: supported. Targets: ORIGINAL-w10::bio-proposal-Barley_Grains.

Singular Barley grain in the sole frozen occurrence denotes the grain input named by the existing plural owner. The primary CCAP PDF calls for one barley grain per25mL before autoclaving; this supports the input-stage grain alias without identifying the later processed material. UNMAPPED_0096, UNMAPPED status, UNDEFINED_MIXTURE type, occurrence counts and absence of an ontology_mapping remain unchanged.

Retained limits: Do not infer species, cultivar, grain mass, flour/extract/straw equivalence, procurement, purity or sterility-at-input from the recipe. Do not conflate with the separately read Barley_Grains_Autoclaved/UNMAPPED_0104 record. Later autoclaving is a process step, not evidence the ingredient was supplied autoclaved. Historical Edison prose remains explicitly provenance-only; no Hordeum taxon or food ontology identity is approved. Retain VARIABLE plus literal one-grain/25mL notes and preparation order. No new external mapping, role or complete recipe approval. A future supported stable-MIM-only identity remains contingent on genuine current native owner/source decisions; this preparation does not allocate or approve it.

