### 17β-Estradiol — complete source candidate transition

identity: supported. Targets: ORIGINAL-w10::chem-proposal-99.

NBRC1181 names the17beta isomer and the captured ChEBI record explicitly defines that isomer as CHEBI:16469, with ASCII label17beta-estradiol. The payload preserves beta stereochemistry rather than identifying generic estradiol or17alpha. The new owner omits the conflicting quantity and does not assert a growth-factor role. SYNONYM_MATCH supports an exact external mapping candidate after genuine native review, independently of source identity/export acceptance. The record marks its new agent mapping evidence LLM_SUGGESTION and its curation history llm_assisted. The #1226 provenance correction explicitly preserves prior source, role and export holds.

Retained limits: NBRC1181 says1mg with1Lwater; the frozen source occurrence says1g/L. Preserve both raw claims and the contradiction, withhold the source export while its holds remain, and do not silently convert or choose a quantity. Nominal ingredient identity does not settle source recipe correctness, whole-source exact identity, growth-factor activity, efficacy or formulation. CREATE_DISTINCT_CONCEPT does not clear residual_other_holds. No hydrate, solvent, supplier, catalogue or purity is inferred. No ontology-parent subclass assertion is created. The bounded ignored-inclusive search found no estradiol/CHEBI16469 owner in LC/data/ingredients or LC/data/curated. This is not a claim about all sources or future TC allocations.

