assessments:
- assessment_id: science_1
  area: identity
  topic: cerium(III) nitrate hexahydrate — complete source candidate transition
  outcome: supported
  summary: MediaDive 1587 supplies the parenthesized Ce(NO3)3 x 6 H2O formula and
    CAS10294-41-4; PubChem CID16211466 independently corroborates cerium(III) nitrate
    hexahydrate, CeH12N3O15, mass434.22 and the exact supplied InChI. The exact-form
    CAS identity, six waters and Ce(III) oxidation state are supported. The MeSH Concept
    M0319657 is the broader Ce(III) nitrate target; NARROW_MATCH must retain skos:broadMatch,
    not exactMatch or subclass_of. Changing the malformed flattened token to REJECTED_LABEL
    preserves its source evidence while preventing it from resolving as an approved
    chemical synonym. The corrected provider token is retained as RAW_TEXT; prior
    history and occurrence statistics are preserved. The payload corrects the earlier
    unresolved formula/CAS gap with inspected evidence and explicitly withdraws inherited
    publication support; its proposed MAPPED status is not itself native review approval.
  target_ids:
  - ORIGINAL-w02::c-proposal-cerium-nitrate-hexahydrate
  evidence_ids:
  - cerium_mediadive
  - cerium_pubchem
  - cerium_pubchem_names
  - cerium_mesh_concept
  - cerium_mesh_record
  - target_1
  - local_policy
  - materialized_source_plan
  dimensions:
  - name: review_role
    value: independent_skeptical
    definition: Reviewer did not author original payloads or current primary assessment.
    evidence_ids:
    - target_1
  - name: review_scope
    value: source_record_transition_only
    definition: Full proposed ingredient and its exact beforeimage; excludes role,
      source export, stable adoption and application authorization.
    evidence_ids:
    - target_1
    - materialized_source_plan
  - name: mapping_scope
    value: Form-specific identity; actual external predicate preserved; no inferred
      subclass or identity collapse.
    definition: Repository mapping semantics govern, not broad-parent equivalence.
    evidence_ids:
    - target_1
    - local_policy
  - name: scientific_status
    value: supported_transition_with_preserved_limits
    definition: Positive scoped scientific assessment of the stated edit only; no
      other hold cleared.
    evidence_ids:
    - cerium_mediadive
    - cerium_pubchem
    - cerium_pubchem_names
    - cerium_mesh_concept
    - cerium_mesh_record
    - target_1
    - local_policy
    - materialized_source_plan
  details: 'Retained limits: No exact ChEBI claim or assertion that no exact ontology
    term exists globally. Captured searches have bounded coverage; the unsupported
    CAS web response is not CAS-authority corroboration. Sigma product comparison
    is evidence of material identity only, not procurement of the original recipe.
    No supplier, catalogue, lot, purity or role is assigned to the source. MediaDive''s
    nominal0.06g/L belongs to a stock solution; DSMZ specifies per litre water, not
    a measured final stock volume. No final-medium dose, or approval of flattened
    medium occurrences, follows. Do not promote all PubChem synonym strings: the captured
    list also contains solution/grade wording beyond this exact hydrate. No Cerium
    export-source binding is introduced in the four-source/five-occurrence export
    canary. Future stable adoption must preserve assigned MIM:0002742 and typed legacy
    record aliases; the rejected bare label must stay non-resolving. This preparation
    does not execute that continuity proof.'
