actions: []
limitations:
- Estradiol source quantity/role/export holds remain.
- MEM whole-source WITHHOLD remains; MEM is not an edited transition here.
- No original campaign scientific or publication hold is cleared.
- Cerium adds no export source binding; all current source provenance and withheld
  accounting must be independently verified after materialization.
- Captured sources were reread locally; no new HTTP or provider call. The archived
  supplier response is not source procurement evidence.
- M0319657 is an NLM Concept; generic descriptor wording in historical notes does
  not change the verified target. No exact ChEBI-absence claim is made.
- Native schema/review persistence checks validate review structure and currentness,
  not chemical truth. No new deterministic ingredient/QC suite was run in this reviewer
  turn; application and release gates remain outstanding.
- Historical external paths inside copied immutable evidence are provenance only.
  All actual local bytes used are explicitly represented in source.inputs under LC.
- Scientific support here is confined to the four source-record transitions. It does
  not approve roles, doses, whole-source identity edges, inherited publication support,
  TC stable IDs or application.
notes:
- Native input-copy materialization is not scientific approval. This report adds an
  actual independent scientific assessment to exact current target bytes.
- Retain original1879-case/1022-origin campaign scope and original scientific holds.
  The four-source/five-occurrence export canary is separate and includes withheld
  MEM; Cerium adds no export-source binding.
